{"raw": {"https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7842": {"title": "Patterson Endowed Professor/Distinguished Scholar", "description": "Elizabeth City State University Jobs | Patterson Endowed Professor/Distinguished Scholar Skip to Main Content Come to Discover . Leave to Conquer . Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help ECSU Home Human Resources Patterson Endowed Professor/Distinguished Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. Posting Details Posting Summary Position Number 6086-0000-0000-165 Classification Title Endowed Professor/ Distinguished Scholar Working Title Patterson Endowed Professor/Distinguished Scholar Division Academic Affairs Department/Unit Department of Mathematics, Computer Science, and Technology Section Engineering Technology Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Mathematics, Computer Science, and Engineering Technology is an academic unit in the School of Science, Aviation, Health, and Technology. The department offers students the Bachelor of Science degree in Engineering Technology, Computer Science, and Mathematics. The purpose of the unit is to foster an environment that encourages students to become active participants in the process of learning by providing quality teaching, advising, and engagement in career explorations. Description of Work The primary purpose of the position is to provide innovative leadership in the area of Engineering Technology. The primary responsibilities of this position will be to facilitate collaborations between the STEM (science, technology, engineering, and mathematics) and secondary school education majors with an interest in STEM , emphasizing the engineering technology fields, and the recruitment and retention of mathematics and science teacher education majors. The professor will apply research -based best practices and cultivate long-term partnerships to stimulate and motivate the next generation of teachers, engineering, and technology professionals. The position will teach, develop, and assess courses. Competencies/Knowledge Skills, and Abilities Required in this Position An earned doctorate in engineering technology or related area with relevant professional experience. Must have a minimum of 18 hours of graduate coursework in an engineering technology-related discipline, with a minimum of three years college level teaching. Must have demonstrated ability to lead student research projects and incorporate experiential learning activities into courses. Minimum Training and Experience A Doctorate degree is required in Engineering Technology or related areas. May hire at the lower rank of Distinguished Scholar based on review of credentials. The individual selected for the Distinguished Professorship will be a published scholar in Engineering Technology . His/her presence on the faculty will provide intellectual depth while further strengthening the quality of teaching in the fulfillment of the university\u2019s mission of excellence in research and scholarly activities. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Management Preferences Position Recruitment Range Position Category Faculty Position Status Permanent Full Time FLSA Exempt Posting Detail Information Posting Number EHRA00616P Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. EHRA OSHR Statement This position is Exempt from the State Human Resources Act. AA/EEO Statement Elizabeth City State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity and expression, political affiliation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information or sexual orientation. Background Check Statement Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University\u2019s receipt of a satisfactory criminal background report. Eligibility for Employment You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran\u2019s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. Elizabeth City State University State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Elizabeth City State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7791 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Are you a current employee of the university? Yes No Do you have a Doctoral degree in Engineering Technology or a related field? Yes No Are you a published scholar in Engineering Technology? Yes No What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts will be required if you are identified as a finalist for the position.) DD214 Other Human Resources Elizabeth City State University 1704 Weeksville Road Elizabeth City, NC 27909 Mainline: 252.335.3252 | Fax: 252.335.3415 www.ecsu.edu University of North Carolina System-wide Employment North Carolina State Government Agencies Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7827": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor", "description": "Elizabeth City State University Jobs | Assistant/Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Come to Discover . Leave to Conquer . Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help ECSU Home Human Resources Assistant/Associate Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. Posting Details Posting Summary Position Number 6086-0000-0000-231 Classification Title Assistant Professor Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor Division Academic Affairs Department/Unit Department of Mathematics, Computer Science, and Technology Section Mathematics Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Division of Academic Affairs provides leadership in developing and maintaining quality academic programs and support services that contribute to the achievement of the university\u2019s mission. The division strives to be recognized as a student-centered university with emphasis on excellence in teaching, learning, and scholarly activities; commitment to total student development; and outstanding service and engagement with local, regional, national and global communities. Description of Work The primary purpose of the position is to teach both general education math courses and upper level courses within the mathematics major. Competencies/Knowledge Skills, and Abilities Required in this Position Must be committed to excellence in student learning and be able to promote students\u2019 ability to succeed in a multicultural and global community. Minimum Training and Experience A Doctorate degree is required. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Management Preferences Doctorate in Mathematics is preferred. A Master\u2019s degree in Mathematics or a Master\u2019s in a related field from a regionally accredited university with a minimum of 18 graduate semester hour credits in Mathematics. Position Recruitment Range Position Category Faculty Position Status Permanent Full Time FLSA Exempt Posting Detail Information Posting Number EHRA00618P Job Open Date 09/04/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the en