Department/Unit Department of Mathematics, Computer Science, and Technology Section Mathematics Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Mathematics, Computer Science, and Engineering Technology is an academic unit in the School of Science, Aviation, Health, and Technology within the Division of Academic Affairs. The department offers undergraduate degrees in Mathematics, Computer Science, and Engineering Technology. The department also offers minors in Mathematics, Computer Science, and Engineering Technology. A Master of Science degree in Mathematics is offered with concentrations in Applied Mathematics, Mathematics Teaching, and Remote Sensing. The purpose of the unit is to foster an environment that encourages students to become active participants in the process of learning by providing quality teaching, advising, and engagement in career explorations.A Doctorate degree is required in mathematics or related areas. The individual selected for the Distinguished Professorship will be a published scholar in mathematics. His/her presence on the faculty will provide intellectual depth while further strengthening the quality of teaching in the fulfillment of the university\u2019s mission of excellence in research and scholarly activities. Description of Work The primary purpose of the position is to raise the prestige and visibility of the university in northeastern North Carolina, the state, and the nation. The distinguished professorship will raise expectations, improve academic excellence, and enhance student learning thereby producing a more competitive ECSU student. The position will teach, develop, and assess courses. Competencies/Knowledge Skills, and Abilities Required in this Position Assist with recruitment and retention of undergraduate and graduate mathematics programs at ECSU . Build partnerships with private, state, and federal agencies to increase external funding in the department. Provide evidence of excellence in research and teaching through published articles and presentations at national conferences. Improve collaborations with industry in northeastern North Carolina, the state and national industrial research facilities to enhance intellectual exchange between ECSU and other stakeholders. Minimum Training and Experience A Doctorate degree is required in mathematics or related areas. May hire at the lower rank of Distinguished Scholar based on review of credentials. The individual selected for the Distinguished Professorship will be a published scholar in mathematics. His/her presence on the faculty will provide intellectual depth while further strengthening the quality of teaching in the fulfillment of the university\u2019s mission of excellence in research and scholarly activities. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Management Preferences Position Recruitment Range Position Category Faculty Position Status Permanent Full Time FLSA Exempt Posting Detail Information Posting Number EHRA00619P Job Open Date 09/08/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. EHRA OSHR Statement This position is Exempt from the State Human Resources Act. AA/EEO Statement Elizabeth City State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity and expression, political affiliation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information or sexual orientation. Background Check Statement Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University\u2019s receipt of a satisfactory criminal background report. Eligibility for Employment You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran\u2019s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. Elizabeth City State University State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Elizabeth City State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7823 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Are you a current employee of the university? Yes No Do you have a Doctorate degree in mathematics or related area? Yes No Are you a published scholar in mathematics? Yes No What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts will be required if you are identified as a finalist for the position.) Optional Documents DD214 Other Human Resources Elizabeth City State University 1704 Weeksville Road Elizabeth City, NC 27909 Mainline: 252.335.3252 | Fax: 252.335.3415 www.ecsu.edu University of North Carolina System-wide Employment North Carolina State Government Agencies Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7809": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Entrepreneurship", "description": "Elizabeth City State University Jobs | Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Entrepreneurship Skip to Main Content Come to Discover . Leave to Conquer . Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help ECSU Home Human Resources Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Entrepreneurship Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. Posting Details Posting Summary Position Number 6086-0000-0000-534 Classification Title Assistant Professor Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Management/Entrepreneurship Division Academic Affairs Department/Unit Department of Business, Accounting, and Sport Management Section Business Administration Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Established in 1891, Elizabeth City State University is a constituent institution of The University of North Carolina. The University currently offers 27 undergraduate and 4 graduate programs of study in fields such as aviation and natural sciences, business administration, accounting, sport management, teaching and, visual and performing arts, mathematics and computer science, social sciences and other select professional and pre-professional areas. Known for its small class sizes and student-centered approach to educating undergraduates the University is located on the beautiful northeastern coast of North Carolina in the Historic town of Elizabeth City. The Division of Academic Affairs provides leadership in developing and maintaining quality academic programs and support services that contribute to the achievement of the university\u2019s mission. The division strives to be recognized as a student-centered university with emphasis on excellence in teaching, learning, and scholarly activities; commitment to total student development; and outstanding service and engagement with local, regional, national and global communities. Description of Work The Department of Business, Accounting and Sport Management at Elizabeth City State University invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track faculty member (Assistant or Associate) in Management. The successful candidate will develop and deliver courses for traditional and virtual classrooms for undergraduate students in the Department. The Department is accredited by AACSB International, and the candidate is expected to meet the initial and sustaining qualifications as Scholarly Academic (SA) or Practicing Academic (PA). The successful applicant will be a dedicated teacher, active scholar, an effective advisor for students with varied background, preparation, and career goals. Competencies/Knowledge Skills, and Abilities Required in this Position A Ph.D. from an accredited academic institution is required in one of the following fields: Management/ Business Administration with an emphasis in management; or a Ph.D. from an accredited academic institution in a closely related field with at least 18 graduate semester credit hours in areas of principles of management, entrepreneurship, leadership and teamwork, organizational behavior, and ethics. ABD doctoral candidates will be considered if the defense of the dissertation is expected to be completed before the start date of employment. Experiences in teaching principles of management, entrepreneurship, leadership and teamwork, organizational behavior, and ethics preferred. Publications in scholarly journals ranked by ABDC or Cabell\u2019s International in the discipline preferred. Ability to teach in other related areas of business-like strategic management, and business research will be a plus. Demonstrate effective communication skills. Possess the ability to write grants and/or conduct and publish research. Possess a commitment to collegiality when interacting with others in a diverse work environment. Possess an enthusiasm for mentoring undergraduate students. Possess a commitment to research and innovative problem-based teaching and experiential learning. Minimum Training and Experience A Doctorate degree is required. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation N/A Management Preferences Position Recruitment Range Position Category Faculty Position Status Permanent Full Time FLSA Exempt Posting Detail Information Posting Number EHRA00617P Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. EHRA OSHR Statement This position is Exempt from the State Human Resources Act. AA/EEO Statement Elizabeth City State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity and expression, political affiliation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information or sexual orientation. Background Check Statement Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University\u2019s receipt of a satisfactory criminal background report. Eligibility for Employment You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran\u2019s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. Elizabeth City State University State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Elizabeth City State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7793 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you a current employee of the university? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Do you have a doctorate degree? Yes No What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts will be required if you are identified as a finalist for the position.) Optional Documents DD214 Other Human Resources Elizabeth City State University 1704 Weeksville Road Elizabeth City, NC 27909 Mainline: 252.335.3252 | Fax: 252.335.3415 www.ecsu.edu University of North Carolina System-wide Employment North Carolina State Government Agencies Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7808": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration - Entrepreneurship", "description": "Elizabeth City State University Jobs | Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration - Entrepreneurship Skip to Main Content Come to Discover . Leave to Conquer . Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help ECSU Home Human Resources Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration - Entrepreneurship Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. Posting Details Posting Summary Position Number 6086-0000-0001-091 Classification Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration-Entrepreneurship Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration - Entrepreneurship Division Academic Affairs Department/Unit Department of Business, Accounting, and Sport Management Section Business Administration Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Division of Academic Affairs provides leadership in developing and maintaining quality academic programs and support services that contribute to the achievement of the university\u2019s mission. The division strives to be recognized as a student-centered university with emphasis on excellence in teaching, learning, and scholarly activities; commitment to total student development; and outstanding service and engagement with local, regional, national and global communities. Description of Work The Department of Business, Accounting and Sport Management at Elizabeth City State University is accredited by AACSB International and invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track faculty member (Assistant/Associate Professor) in Entrepreneurship and Management. This position will develop and deliver courses for traditional and virtual classrooms for undergraduate students in the Department and will teach undergraduate courses with emphasis in experiential learning; engage in relevant research and publish in quality outlets; advise students for academic preparation, career, and graduate school; provide service to the Department, University, and Profession; and develop collaborative relationships with the community. Possess effective communication skills; ability to write grants and/or conduct and publish research. Demonstrate a commitment to collegiality and diverse work environments when interacting with others within the university community Competencies/Knowledge Skills, and Abilities Required in this Position Possess an enthusiasm for mentoring undergraduate students in research projects and experience in using innovative, problem-based teaching and experiential learning. Possess a commitment to excellence in student learning and be able to promote students\u2019 ability to succeed in a multicultural and global community. Possess a research background that complements the existing diversity of research by the departmental faculty. Minimum Training and Experience Minimum Training and Experience: Possess a Doctorate in Management and Entrepreneurship. Degrees must be from AACSB accredited institutions, or Doctorate from an accredited institution in a closely related field with at least 18 graduate semester credit hours relevant to Management and Entrepreneurship. ABD doctoral candidates will be considered if the dissertation defense is expected to be completed before the start date of employment. Meet the initial and sustaining qualifications as Scholarly Academic (SA) or Practicing Academic (PA). Experiences in teaching entrepreneurship, strategic management, ethics, and management. The ability to teach in other related areas of business and management is a plus. Experience in teaching at a four-year college or university and publications in scholarly journals ranked by ABDC or Cabell\u2019s International in the discipline are preferred. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Management Preferences Position Recruitment Range Position Category Faculty Position Status Permanent Full Time FLSA Exempt Posting Detail Information Posting Number EHRA00614P Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. EHRA OSHR Statement This position is Exempt from the State Human Resources Act. AA/EEO Statement Elizabeth City State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity and expression, political affiliation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information or sexual orientation. Background Check Statement Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University\u2019s receipt of a satisfactory criminal background report. Eligibility for Employment You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran\u2019s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. Elizabeth City State University State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Elizabeth City State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7792 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Are you a current employee of the university? Yes No Do you possess a doctorate in Management and Entrepreneurship from an AACSB-accredited institution? Yes No Do you have a doctorate from an accredited institution in a closely related field with at least 18 graduate semester credit hours relevant to Management and Entrepreneurship? Yes No What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts will be required if you are identified as a finalist for the position.) DD214 Other Human Resources Elizabeth City State University 1704 Weeksville Road Elizabeth City, NC 27909 Mainline: 252.335.3252 | Fax: 252.335.3415 www.ecsu.edu University of North Carolina System-wide Employment North Carolina State Government Agencies Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7782": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor", "description": "Elizabeth City State University Jobs | Assistant/Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Come to Discover . Leave to Conquer . Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help ECSU Home Human Resources Assistant/Associate Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. Posting Details Posting Summary Position Number 6086-0000-0001-038 Classification Title Assistant/Associate Professor Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor Division Academic Affairs Department/Unit Department of Protective and Human Studies Section Kinesiology Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Kinesiology Program is a strong campus program and is home to all Health, Physical Education, Public Health, and the Bachelor of Science in Kinesiology degree, which has three concentrations (1) Exercise Science, (2) Fitness and Wellness, and (3) Physical Education and Health. The Kinesiology Program trains evidence-based leaders and practitioners in the sub-fields of Kinesiology according to ACSM and NSCA standards, preparing students to meet the needs of individuals who are healthy, at risk, or who have known disease(s). The Kinesiology degree competitively prepares students to pursue advanced graduate degrees in disciplines such as athletic training, physical therapy, public health, occupational therapy, fitness and wellness, and allied health professions. Description of Work The Department houses the Kinesiology Program and seeks to hire a faculty with expertise in Exercise Science with an emphasis on Health and Wellness Promotion. Competencies/Knowledge Skills, and Abilities Required in this Position The successful candidate will be expected to establish externally funded research program utilizing existing laboratories and resources at the University to contribute to research, teaching, advising, and community service needs of the Department and University. Teaching undergraduate courses related to exercise science, athletic training, and Health and wellness promotion (e.g., introduction to exercise science, prevention, and care of athletic injuries, applied strength and conditioning, wellness programming and administration, health coaching ). Minimum Training and Experience Doctoral degree in Kinesiology, Health and Wellness Promotion or related disciplines. Track record of scholarly activity commensurate with appointment at the Assistant/Associate Professor rank by the anticipated date of appointment (ABD\u2019s will be considered). Demonstrable evidence of preparedness to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the discipline and establish an independent research program License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Licenses and certifications that align with areas of professional expertise and interest are required. Management Preferences Position Recruitment Range Position Category Faculty Position Status Permanent Full Time FLSA Posting Detail Information Posting Number EHRA00611P Job Open Date 08/10/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. EHRA OSHR Statement This position is Exempt from the State Human Resources Act. AA/EEO Statement Elizabeth City State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity and expression, political affiliation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information or sexual orientation. Background Check Statement Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University\u2019s receipt of a satisfactory criminal background report. Eligibility for Employment You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran\u2019s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. Elizabeth City State University State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Elizabeth City State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7761 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you a current employee of the university? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Do you have a Doctoral degree in Kinesiology, Health and Wellness Promotion, or related disciplines? Yes No Do you have a track record of scholarly activity commensurate with appointment at the Assistant/Associate Professor rank by the anticipated date of appointment? Yes No Do you have demonstrable evidence of preparedness to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the discipline and establish an independent research program? Yes No Do you have licenses and certifications that align with areas of professional expertise and interest? Yes No What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts will be required if you are identified as a finalist for the position.) Optional Documents Other DD214 Human Resources Elizabeth City State University 1704 Weeksville Road Elizabeth City, NC 27909 Mainline: 252.335.3252 | Fax: 252.335.3415 www.ecsu.edu University of North Carolina System-wide Employment North Carolina State Government Agencies Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7751": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration", "description": "Elizabeth City State University Jobs | Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration Skip to Main Content Come to Discover . Leave to Conquer . Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help ECSU Home Human Resources Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. Posting Details Posting Summary Position Number 6086-0000-0000-590 Classification Title Assistant Professor Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Administration Division Academic Affairs Department/Unit Department of Business, Accounting, and Sport Management Section Department of Business, Accounting, and Sport Management (section) Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Division of Academic Affairs provides leadership in developing and maintaining quality academic programs and support services that contribute to the achievement of the university\u2019s mission. The division strives to be recognized as a student-centered university with emphasis on excellence in teaching, learning, and scholarly activities; commitment to total student development; and outstanding service and engagement with local, regional, national and global communities. Description of Work The Department of Business, Accounting and Sport Management at Elizabeth City State University is accredited by AACSB International and invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track faculty member (Assistant/Associate Professor) in Management. This position will develop and deliver courses for traditional and virtual classrooms for undergraduate students in the Department and will teach undergraduate courses with emphasis in experiential learning; engage in relevant research and publish in quality outlets; advise students for academic preparation, career, and graduate school; provide service to the Department, University, and Profession; and develop collaborative relationships with the community. Competencies/Knowledge Skills, and Abilities Required in this Position Possess effective communication skills; ability to write grants and/or conduct and publish research. Demonstrate a commitment to collegiality and diverse work environments when interacting with others within the university community. Possess an enthusiasm for mentoring undergraduate students in research projects and experience in using innovative, problem-based teaching and experiential learning. Possess a commitment to excellence in student learning and be able to promote students\u2019 ability to succeed in a multicultural and global community. Possess a research background that complements the existing diversity of research by the departmental faculty. Minimum Training and Experience A Doctorate degree is required for the rank of Assistant Professor. May hire at the rank of Lecturer with a master\u2019s degree from a regionally accredited university with a minimum of 18 graduate semester hour credits in relevant field and three years college level teaching. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Management Preferences Position Recruitment Range Position Category Faculty Position Status Permanent Full Time FLSA Exempt Posting Detail Information Posting Number EHRA00606P Job Open Date 07/20/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. EHRA OSHR Statement This position is Exempt from the State Human Resources Act. AA/EEO Statement Elizabeth City State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity and expression, political affiliation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information or sexual orientation. Background Check Statement Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University\u2019s receipt of a satisfactory criminal background report. Eligibility for Employment You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran\u2019s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. Elizabeth City State University State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Elizabeth City State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7739 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Are you a current employee of the university? Yes No Do you have a Doctorate degree? Yes No Do you have a master\u2019s degree from a regionally accredited university with a minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in a relevant field and three years of college-level teaching? Yes No What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts will be required if you are identified as a finalist for the position.) Optional Documents DD214 Other Human Resources Elizabeth City State University 1704 Weeksville Road Elizabeth City, NC 27909 Mainline: 252.335.3252 | Fax: 252.335.3415 www.ecsu.edu University of North Carolina System-wide Employment North Carolina State Government Agencies Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7749": {"title": "E. V. Wilkins Endowed Professor/ Distinguished Scholar", "description": "Elizabeth City State University Jobs | E. V. Wilkins Endowed Professor/ Distinguished Scholar Skip to Main Content Come to Discover . Leave to Conquer . Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help ECSU Home Human Resources E. V. Wilkins Endowed Professor/ Distinguished Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. Posting Details Posting Summary Position Number 6086-0000-0001-102 Classification Title Endowed Professor/ Distinguished Scholar Working Title E. V. Wilkins Endowed Professor/ Distinguished Scholar Division Academic Affairs Department/Unit Department of Education Section Education Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Division of Academic Affairs provides leadership in developing and maintaining quality academic programs and support services that contribute to the achievement of the university\u2019s mission. The division strives to be recognized as a student-centered university with emphasis on excellence in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; commitment to total student development; and outstanding service and engagement with local, regional, national and global communities. Description of Work This Endowed Professor will support existing programs and activities of the department and provide leadership for the following initiatives: development of a rural teacher/administrative training program in collaboration with rural school districts and communities; establishment of summer institutes and professional development opportunities for P-12 teachers, administrators, school boards and other community stakeholders; and development and teaching of advanced training programs. In addition, the chair will continue to pursue scholarly activities and secure external funds to support initiatives; serve on university, local and state committees, boards, task forces and make in-service presentations to community constituents, etc. Competencies/Knowledge Skills, and Abilities Required in this Position Possess an established record of accomplishments and contributions to the field of education and professional activity reflected by publications, grants, and national prominence in teacher education. An established scholar with demonstrated experience in the integration of technology and knowledge in personnel preparation in high needs areas of teacher education. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills are essential for establishing a wide array of effective working relationships within and outside the campus community. Minimum Training and Experience A Doctorate degree is required in Education or related areas. May hire at the lower rank of Distinguished Scholar based on review of credentials. The individual selected for the Distinguished Professorship will be a published scholar in Education . His/her presence on the faculty will provide intellectual depth while further strengthening the quality of teaching in the fulfillment of the university\u2019s mission of excellence in research and scholarly activities. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation Management Preferences Position Recruitment Range Position Category Faculty Position Status Permanent Full Time FLSA Exempt Posting Detail Information Posting Number EHRA00607P Job Open Date 07/20/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant \u2022 Please ensure your full range of knowledge, skills, abilities, experience, and education are listed on your application. Do not write \u2018see resume\u2019 on your application when completing the job duties section. \u2022 If you answer the supplemental questions at the end of the application, please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers. EHRA OSHR Statement This position is Exempt from the State Human Resources Act. AA/EEO Statement Elizabeth City State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity and expression, political affiliation, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information or sexual orientation. Background Check Statement Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University\u2019s receipt of a satisfactory criminal background report. Eligibility for Employment You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran\u2019s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. Elizabeth City State University State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Elizabeth City State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7738 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other * Are you a current employee of the university? Yes No * Do you have a doctorate degree in Education or related areas? Yes No * Are you a published scholar in Education? Yes No * What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/ Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts will be required if you are identified as a finalist for the position.) Optional Documents DD214 Other Human Resources Elizabeth City State University 1704 Weeksville Road Elizabeth City, NC 27909 Mainline: 252.335.3252 | Fax: 252.335.3415 www.ecsu.edu University of North Carolina System-wide Employment North Carolina State Government Agencies Employment To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.ecsu.edu/postings/7741": {"title": "Adjunct", "description": "Elizabeth City State University Jobs | Adjunct Skip to Main Content